/*!
\page page_stssdhit StSsdHit

\ref StSsdHit represents a single reconstructed space-point hit in the STAR Silicon Strip
Detector (SSD), a double-sided silicon strip detector providing P-side and N-side strip
measurements.  A hit arises from the coincidence of a cluster on each side.

\see StSsdHitCollection

\section sec_ssdhit_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\verbatim
StObject
└── StMeasuredPoint
    └── StHit
        └── StSsdHit
\endverbatim

Hits are collected in \ref StSsdHitCollection.

\section sec_ssdhit_members Data Members

\subsection subsec_ssdhit_inherited Inherited from StHit

- <tt>UInt_t mHardwarePosition</tt> — Packed hardware word.  Bits 4–12: flat wafer index.
  Bits 13–22: N-side central strip.  Bits 23–27: P-side offset relative to N-side.
  Bits 28–29: N-side cluster size − 1.  Bits 30–31: P-side cluster size − 1.
- <tt>StThreeVectorF mPositionError</tt> — 1-σ errors in STAR global frame (cm). <em>Not persisted.</em>
- <tt>Float_t mCharge</tt> — Cluster charge (ADC counts).
- <tt>Int_t mId</tt> — Cluster identifier.
- <tt>Int_t mIdTruth</tt> — Geant track ID (simulation only).
- <tt>UShort_t mQuality</tt> — Charge fraction from <tt>mIdTruth</tt> (percent).
- <tt>UChar_t mFitFlag</tt> — Non-zero if used in a track fit.
- <tt>UChar_t mTrackRefCount</tt> — Number of tracks referencing this hit.
- <tt>UShort_t mFlag</tt> — Hit status flag bitmask.

\subsection subsec_ssdhit_own Own Data Members

- <tt>Float_t mLocalPosition[2]</tt> — Local hit position (cm): [0] = P-side strip direction,
  [1] = N-side strip direction.
- <tt>static StMemoryPool mPool</tt> — Per-class memory pool. <em>Not persisted.</em>

\section sec_ssdhit_geometry Geometry

The SSD has 20 ladders (1–20), each with 16 wafers (1–16), grouped into 4 sectors:

| Ladders   | Sector |
|-----------|--------|
| 1–2, 20   | 1      |
| 3–9       | 2      |
| 10–12     | 3      |
| 13–19     | 4      |

<b>volumeID</b> = <tt>10000 × sector + 7000 + 100 × wafer + ladder</tt>.

\section sec_ssdhit_methods Key Methods

- <tt>unsigned int ladder() const</tt> — Ladder number (1–20).
- <tt>unsigned int wafer() const</tt> — Wafer number (1–16).
- <tt>unsigned int sector() const</tt> — Sector (1–4).
- <tt>unsigned int centralStripNSide() const</tt> — N-side central strip index.
- <tt>unsigned int centralStripPSide() const</tt> — P-side central strip index.
- <tt>unsigned int clusterSizeNSide() const</tt> — N-side cluster size.
- <tt>unsigned int clusterSizePSide() const</tt> — P-side cluster size.
- <tt>float localPosition(unsigned int i) const</tt> — Local coordinate along axis <tt>i</tt> (cm).
- <tt>void setLocalPosition(float u, float v)</tt> — Set local position (cm).
- <tt>virtual int volumeID() const</tt> — Packed geometry ID.
- <tt>StDetectorId detector() const</tt> — Returns the detector ID from bits 0–3 of <tt>mHardwarePosition</tt>.

\section sec_ssdhit_ownership Object Ownership

\ref StSsdHit uses a custom <tt>StMemoryPool</tt> allocator.  Once added to
\ref StSsdHitCollection, ownership belongs to the framework.
\warning Do <b>not</b> <tt>delete</tt> \ref StSsdHit pointers obtained from the collection.

\section sec_ssdhit_usage Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
StSsdHitCollection* ssdColl = event->ssdHitCollection();
if (!ssdColl) return;

for (unsigned int iLadder = 0; iLadder < ssdColl->numberOfLadders(); ++iLadder) {
    const StSsdLadderHitCollection* ladder = ssdColl->ladder(iLadder);
    if (!ladder) continue;
    for (unsigned int iWafer = 0; iWafer < ladder->numberOfWafers(); ++iWafer) {
        const StSsdWaferHitCollection* wafer = ladder->wafer(iWafer);
        if (!wafer) continue;
        const StSPtrVecSsdHit& hits = wafer->hits();
        for (const StSsdHit* hit : hits) {
            float localP = hit->localPosition(0);   // P-side (cm)
            float localN = hit->localPosition(1);   // N-side (cm)
        }
    }
}
\endcode

*/
